{
  "id": "COMPOUND:24764 - PROTEIN:569",
  "verbalization": "Garcinielliptone L is implicated in the target pathway of 3 beta-hydroxysteroid dehydrogenase/Delta 5-->4-isomerase type 1 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Garcinielliptone L directly targets Aldehyde dehydrogenase, mitochondrial, which in turn is targeted by 3,4-Dihydroxycinnamic Acid. This chain of targets ultimately leads to the enzyme 3 beta-hydroxysteroid dehydrogenase/Delta 5-->4-isomerase type 1. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for Garcinielliptone L in modulating the activity of this enzyme, possibly through the regulation of aldehyde dehydrogenase, which is a critical step in steroid metabolism. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Garcinielliptone L and the enzyme, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
